    "sixtySeconds": {
      "whatItDoes": "llamafile lets you distribute and run large language models as one file. It combines llama.cpp with Cosmopolitan Libc so a model and its runtime become a single executable that runs locally on most operating systems and CPU architectures. It also includes whisperfile, a single-file speech-to-text tool built on whisper.cpp.",
      "problem": "Running a local LLM usually means installing runtimes and dependencies. With llamafile you download one file and run it.",
      "whoFor": [
        "Beginners trying local AI",
        "Developers distributing models to users",
        "Privacy-minded people who want offline AI"
      ],
      "whyChoose": "Choose it for the simplest possible local LLM experience, from Mozilla, on almost any OS.",
      "requirements": [
        "macOS, Linux, BSD or Windows",
        "Enough memory for the model you pick"
      ]
    },
    "overview": [
      "Download a prebuilt llamafile, such as the small Qwen3.5 0.8B example, make it executable on macOS, Linux or BSD, and run it. On Windows, rename it to end in .exe.",
      "Windows can only run executables under 4GB, so for bigger models download the llamafile binary and run it with external weights. Larger models give better answers if your hardware allows.",
      "Versions from 0.10.0 use a new build system aligned with recent llama.cpp, so some older features may be missing. The project is Apache 2.0; its changes to llama.cpp and whisper.cpp are MIT."
